\section*{Results}
\subsection*{Results already available from our codes (fcc(111), PRL 2012 protocol)}
Five fcc(111) surfaces of this paper (Cu, Rh, Au, Pt, Pd) were already computed with our codes for the recreation of
PRL 108, 126402 (2012) (Al(111) report, Tables~2--4). Table~\ref{tab:exist} compares them with
Ref.~\cite{Patra2020}. Protocol of these runs (differs from Ref.~\cite{Patra2020} and from the full runs below):
self-consistent LDA, PBE, PBEsol, Q2D-GGA at the PRL lattice constants, 11-layer unrelaxed slabs, 10~\AA\ vacuum,
$10\times10\times1$ $k$ points, three-layer bulk (\texttt{codes/PRL2012\_scf/prl2012\_scf.py}); SCAN and DC-SCAN to
first order on the self-consistent PBEsol density, $\sigma^{F}\approx\sigma^{\rm PBEsol}+\Delta\sigma_{xc}^{F-{\rm PBEsol}}$,
8-layer slabs, 14~\AA\ vacuum (\texttt{codes/Al/22\_surface\_density\_dcscan.py}). Table~\ref{tab:existlat} gives the
lattice constants of the same metals (\texttt{codes/PRL2012\_scf/lattice\_scf.py}, Birch--Murnaghan fit).
