\subsection*{Full reproduction of Ref.~\cite{Patra2020} (protocol above)}
\paragraph{Density cutoff per metal (completed for @NGATE@ metals).} Primitive bulk at the experimental lattice
constant, $6\times6\times6$ $k$ points, cutoffs 150, 250, 350, 450 and 600~Ha, Q2D-GGA and SCAN (the most
grid-sensitive functionals of this work). The chosen cutoff is the smallest with FFT-gradient error $<1\%$,
$|N_{\rm grid}-N|<10^{-4}$ and $|E-E(600~{\rm Ha})|<1$~meV/atom for both functionals (the criteria of the cutoff gate
of the PRL recreation); Table~\ref{tab:gate} lists the error measures at the chosen cutoff. Fe and Co (spin-polarised):
energy criterion only; their gate ran with independent ferromagnetic starts, whose energies scatter by 1--7~mHa/atom,
so the conservative 600~Ha is used (lattice and surface runs follow one magnetic solution, see the code).

\paragraph{Equilibrium lattice constants (@NLAT@ of @NLATTOT@ scans complete).} Each functional at its own
equilibrium lattice constant (as in Ref.~\cite{Patra2020}), from nine self-consistent bulk energies within
